     \"summary\": \"#10642 Support for org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5; label=library-new-request; body_chars=61\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"existing_tests\",\n        \"summary\": \"0 existing test file path(s) included\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"input_tokens_used\": 34,\n    \"issue_label\": \"library-new-request\",\n    \"issue_number\": 10642,\n    \"library\": \"org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5\",\n    \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n    \"output_tokens_used\": 16603,\n    \"risks\": [\n      \"Pulsar standalone's startup is slower and more resource-hungry than the other broker images already allow-listed (nats, rabbitmq), which may increase test wall-clock time and flakiness risk under constrained CI resources.\",\n      \"pulsar-client-all is a large shaded jar (~hundreds of MB transitively: netty, avro, protobuf, bouncycastle); native-image build time/memory could be heavier than typical libraries in this repo \\u2014 no specific blocking GraalVM issue was found during research, but local Gradle/native-image verification remains authoritative.\"\n    ],\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"summary\": \"pulsar-client-all needs a live broker for meaningful producer/consumer coverage; no extra Maven dependency required since the uber-jar resolves its own transitives.\"\n  },\n  \"libraryUpdateRoute\": null,\n  \"newVersion\": null,\n  \"phases\": {\n    \"explore\": {\n      \"chunkClassCount\": null,\n      \"chunkProcessedClassCount\": 0,\n      \"exhaustedClasses\": [],\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"status\": \"running\"\n    },\n    \"finalization\": {\n      \"status\": \"pending\"\n    },\n    \"fix\": {\n      \"iteration\": null,\n      \"status\": \"skipped\"\n    },\n    \"publication\": {\n      \"branch\": null,\n      \"coverageFollowUpIssueNumber\": null,\n      \"isPushed\": false,\n      \"publicationId\": null,\n      \"publicationTimestamp\": null,\n      \"status\": \"pending\"\n    },\n    \"setup\": {\n      \"