hema registration and ZSTD-compressed round-trip.\n- Byte-message reading from the earliest message with keys, properties, and sequence IDs.\n\nAdded coverage for Pulsar’s separated key/value schema:\n\n- Uses `Schema.KeyValue(..., KeyValueEncodingType.SEPARATED)`.\n- Sends through a real producer and receives through a real consumer.\n- Verifies the separately encoded key and decoded key/value pair.\n- Acknowledges the received message.\n\nNo metadata was changed because the reporter context names no explicit missing metadata requirement. Per instruction, tests were not compiled or run. `git diff --check` passes.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cff9277becaa1b9016ad0967d6fc087d1a42ce46ec9ca2fdc\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 582, "output": 480, "cacheRead": 86656, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 281, "totalTokens": 87718, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1792054899005, "responseId": "resp_0cff9277becaa1b9016ad096746ddc87d1911c21de3f132250", "rawStopReason": "completed"}}
